extends Node2D
class_name CombatView
## Combat.tscn root. Owns exactly one CombatEngine instance per combat (architecture plan
## §3/§4: CombatEngine is not an autoload, `.new()` per trận) and NEVER contains game rules
## itself — every gameplay action goes through CombatEngine's public API
## (`use_die`/`reroll_dice`/`end_turn`); this file only listens to EventBus and forwards input.
##
## LAYOUT REWRITE (review-uiux-battle-screen.md, applied 2026-09-17 — see task report for the
## full P0/P1/P2 breakdown): the fixed EnemyBand/BottomBand card rows are gone. Every unit now
## gets a feet-anchored Nameplate (UnitPortrait.gd — name+HP+shield) and a head-anchored
## UnitHeadHUD (status icons, + enemy intent badge) positioned every frame in
## _layout_unit_visuals() using CombatStage3D.get_unit_screen_pos(). The dice tray, mana
## cluster, turn banner, and reroll/end-turn buttons are restyled to the Dango palette
## (the old Dango theme) and the raw dev log is now hidden behind a toggle button, with a separate
## 3-line player-facing translation feed (_append_player_log()) using plain-language Vietnamese
## sentences instead of "[use] X -> Y (part/type)" debug syntax.
##
## STATE-READ DISCIPLINE (architecture plan §4): every EventBus handler below is funneled
## through the ONE function `_rebuild_all()`, the only place that reads `_combat` fields
## directly. `_layout_unit_visuals()` (called from `_process()`, not an EventBus handler) is the
## one deliberate exception — it re-reads `_combat`/CombatStage3D every frame purely to follow
## camera-space positions (idle bob, etc.), never to change what is displayed as game state.
##
## HEADLESS TEST MODE (`disable_juice_for_tests`): unchanged from the pre-review pass — every
## juice entry point (Tweens, the die roll-bounce/lift/flip, hit-stop+shake) checks this flag
## first and, if true, jumps straight to the final state with zero animation. Sets by
## t_combatview_smoke.gd/t_face_used_log_tag.gd before instantiating Combat.tscn.
##
## INPUT MODEL: click-click (dice tray selects source, clicking a Nameplate/3D model selects
## target) — unchanged from the pre-review pass; see CombatStage3D.gd's unit_clicked signal
## comment for the second (3D-model) input path.
##
## DEVIATIONS FROM THE LITERAL REVIEW WORDING (flagged per collaboration protocol — see task
## report for the full list):
##   1. Font: review specifies "Work Sans"; no font asset ships in this repo, so every new
##      Label falls back to Godot's default theme font (the old Dango theme FONT is the single future
##      choke point — see that file's header).
##   2. "Badge mana" (review P1 #6, "die không đủ mana thì xám + badge đỏ"): this engine has no
##      per-die mana COST — mana is a resource generated by "mana"-type faces, never spent to
##      legalize using a die (combat_engine.gd use_die()/_exec_face() gate on roll/used state
##      only). Reinterpreted as: the per-die VALUE badge is unified to one neutral color
##      (was per-face-type colored, which is what the review was actually describing) and a die
##      that is not currently playable (dead/unrolled/already used) greys out — same disabled
##      state this pass already had, just now visually distinct from "used this turn" (which
##      flips face-down instead).
##   3. Damage-preview hover (P0 #2) is wired two ways given the click-click input model has no
##      natural "hovering a target before selecting a die" moment: hovering an unselected,
##      currently-rollable ATTACK die previews its value on every alive enemy; hovering an
##      enemy's intent badge (when that intent is a `dmg` face) previews it on that intent's
##      actual target ally. Both reuse the same HPBar.set_preview() API.
##   4. Drag-and-drop targeting / hit-stop juice repositioning to the new nameplate anchors
##      (review "Đợt 3") is NOT done this pass — flagged as remaining P2 scope in the report.

